[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-PLACE-MIGRATION
TITLE: The scripted pass that gives the existing narratives their PLACE, the Start cards, the reference and source lines, and short tab titles
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
One script over the semantic-layer tree, through the scribe: PLACE on the
five tabs, the sheet snapshot as a tab, the legend as a card, the type,
topic and gap narratives as screens; new cards under the root for what v1's
Start showed -- the heat strip over Topics, the type grid over a grid card
under Types, the layer stack, the five gaps over Gaps, the source facts;
a ladders card under Types; a section under Edges that mirrors the
allowed-edges topic; the 145 topic rows rewritten to headline, reference
line and source line; the legend rows given their by-line labels; the five
tab titles shortened to one word. The type cards move to the spec with
their plan citations turned into inline links. Nothing is signed, so every
edit is free; every new citation is a placeholder.
<<<
